  "description": "This race will determine the U.S. House representative for Wisconsin's 4th Congressional District, which encompasses Milwaukee County and northern Milwaukee suburbs. Incumbent Democrat Gwen Moore, first elected in 2004 and the first African American to represent Wisconsin in Congress, is seeking a 12th term. The district has not elected a Republican since 2004 and is rated Safe/Solid Democratic by major election forecasters. The August 11, 2026 primary will narrow a multi-candidate Democratic field that includes Moore, genetic counselor Amy Donahue, and business development manager Asher Smale; Republican Purnima Nath is running unopposed in her primary; independent candidates Arthur Burks, Carlos Dixon, and Nathan Billips are also on the general election ballot.",
